# The lines the Slang twin of default/main.vert may declare differently from the GLSL (task 0072, stage f), read by
# SlangPermutations in components-tests: "[<define set>] glsl-only: <line>"; every listed line must occur, so a stale
# entry fails the test. All of them are declarations the GLSL keeps and never reads (glslang keeps them, slangc drops
# them); a pipeline may supply attributes and bindings a shader does not read, so nothing the pipeline builds changes.
# Specialization constants that nothing reads (texmatUv without TEXMAT) need no line (vsgUtil::readSpirvInterface).
#
# MORPH: the vertex position input (location 0); the positions come from the morph buffer.
# PARTICLE without NORMAL: the scene uniform and the point light buffers (set 0, bindings 0 and 2 to 5), which only the
#   vertex lighting of NORMAL reads.
